---
// Figure 8: what each remedy for a hot key does to the load on twelve shards.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './cluster.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="cluster-remedies" title="Four answers to a hot key, on twelve shards" controls="none"
  caption="Illustrative model, not a measurement: the model of the figure ‘One hot key, and the shard that holds it’ at 12 shards and Zipf s = 1. Copies: the 10 hottest keys stored as 4 keys each, product:0:0 to product:0:3 and so on, each read choosing one at random. Replicas: one replica per shard, reads split evenly between primary and replica. Near cache: 40 application processes each keep the 1,000 hottest keys for one second. Left out: the cost of writing copies, replication lag, and the memory each remedy uses.">
  <Fragment slot="params">
    <Choice name="remedy" label="Remedy" value="none"
      options={[{ value: 'none', label: 'none' }, { value: 'copies', label: 'copies of hot keys' }, { value: 'replicas', label: 'read from replicas' }, { value: 'near', label: 'near cache' }]} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="busiest" label="Busiest node, reads a second" kind="redis" />
    <Readout name="nodes" label="Redis nodes" kind="neutral" />
    <Readout name="redis" label="Reads reaching Redis" kind="write" />
    <Readout name="usable" label="Usable share of capacity" kind="hit" />
  </Fragment>
  <div data-columns></div>
  <p class="cluster-hot-key" aria-hidden="true"><i></i>reads of the single hottest key<span><b>✕</b> a node over its capacity</span></p>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>With no remedy, the busiest of 12 nodes takes about 100,000 reads a second against an average of 50,000, and about 49,600 of those are the hottest key's. Storing the 10 hottest keys as 4 copies each, on different slots, spreads the hottest key's reads over four nodes, about 12,400 each, brings the busiest node down to about 56,000 and makes 89% of capacity usable, at the cost of 30 extra keys to write. Reading from one replica per shard halves every node's load, the hottest key's included, busiest about 50,000, but doubles the number of nodes, so the usable share stays at 50%. A near cache in each of 40 application processes, holding the 1,000 hottest keys for one second, cuts the reads reaching Redis from 600,000 to about 270,000 a second and leaves the busiest node at about 23,000, close to the average; the hottest key now sends Redis only 40 reads a second.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { bindParams, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { columnChart } from './columns.mjs';
  import { nodeLoads, CAPACITY } from './hotshard-model.mjs';

  const k = (v: number) => `${Math.round(v / 1000)}k`;
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="cluster-remedies"]').forEach(root => {
    const chart = columnChart(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-columns]')!, {
      label: 'Reads a second arriving at each Redis node, with one node’s capacity as a line', capacity: CAPACITY, top: 120000,
    });
    bindParams(root, (params: any) => {
      const r = nodeLoads({ shards: 12, s: 1, remedy: params.remedy });
      chart.set(r);
      setReadouts(root, { busiest: k(r.max), nodes: String(r.nodes), redis: `${k(r.redisReads)} a second`, usable: `${Math.round(r.usable * 100)}%` });
    });
  });
</script>
